WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.510
This is a private dictation app.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.970
Every word is transcribed on your own computer,

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.230
so the recording never has to leave it.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.990
You can record from the microphone, choose a file, or paste a link to a video.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.710
Here, I'm choosing a short audio clip from my computer.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:24.240
It transcribes on the graphics card, and the app tells you so: no network.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.050
So I checked.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.730
While it was transcribing,

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.690
I sampled every network connection held by the app and its web view.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.230
The app's own process opened none.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.650
The one connection came from Microsoft's web view runtime,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.390
the browser engine that draws the interface, and it went to a Microsoft address.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.120
Every word gets its own timestamp, and the whole transcript is editable.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.640
Whisper heard one name wrong, so I fix it right in place.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:01:00.350
Then it exports to plain text, subtitles, Word, PDF, or one zip file of everything.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.390
One Rust core, four backends, and three desktop platforms.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.150
I built it with Jimmy Ong.
